#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""
clientst0r Office service helper: runs this deployment's one managed
ONLYOFFICE Docs container ("Managed Local ONLYOFFICE").

It is a separate root program from clientst0r-root-helper on purpose (see
docs/office/MANAGED_LOCAL.md, "Why a separate helper"):

* it is reached over a Unix socket that systemd owns
  (clientst0r-office-helper.socket, SocketUser=<app user>, SocketMode=0600),
  one short-lived process per connection (Accept=yes). The peer's uid is
  checked with SO_PEERCRED as well;
* the app sends ONE small JSON request: an operation name from a fixed list
  and, for two operations, one validated scalar. It never sends images,
  Compose YAML, paths, volume mounts, environment variables or commands.
  Everything else comes from the root-owned configuration
  /etc/clientst0r/office-service.conf and from the release list compiled
  into this file;
* long operations (install, update, ...) keep running in this process after
  the reply, so a web-worker restart or an app deploy cannot cut them in
  half; their journal lives in a root-owned state directory and an
  interrupted one is detected and reported, never silently resumed;
* it touches only its own Compose project, container, network, firewall
  table and directories. It never installs, upgrades or reconfigures Docker
  itself (scripts/office/install-editor.sh --mode managed-local does the
  prerequisites, run by an administrator).

Operations over the socket (the app's vocabulary, nothing else):

    preflight            read-only host checks
    status               state, health, versions, resources, last operation
    releases             the tested release list and what is installed
    install              create/converge the container (idempotent)
    start | stop | restart
    update  {"release": "<id from the release list>"}
    rollback             back to the release before the last update, from
                         the backup taken by that update
    logs    {"lines": 1..500}   bounded, redacted container log
    uninstall            remove the container; documents, editor data,
                         secrets and backups are kept
    secret               the JWT secret, to the app user only (for the
                         ONLYOFFICE provider settings); never logged

Administrator-only, from a root shell (never over the socket):

    clientst0r-office-helper cli <operation> [...]   any of the above
    clientst0r-office-helper cli purge --confirm <DEPLOYMENT_ID>
    clientst0r-office-helper cli apply-firewall      (also run at boot)

Files:
    /etc/clientst0r/office-service.conf   root-owned settings (see the
                                          .example next to this file)
    /etc/clientst0r/office/               root-only secrets (0700)
    /var/lib/clientst0r-office/           data, compose file, state, backups
    /run/clientst0r-office/               socket and operation lock
"""
